I built the issue desk in plain TypeScript and DOM under `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/desk9-vanilla-haiku-3/src/`: `main.ts` (mount and tabs), `issues.ts`, `help.ts`, `settings.ts`, `store.ts` (shared open-issue count and list answers), and `dom.ts`. `./check` passes and all 30 visible tests pass (2 of 15 runs used). I was unsure about a few points: the assign error reads `assign error: declined` (the brief's "the server's message (`declined`)" was ambiguous); assign, post and label-add do nothing when the user name or label is empty; the related-hit click re-runs the help search as a typed query would; and the one console 404 is probably the browser's favicon request, which I did not confirm.